Decision: keep SandpitRecord as a first-class schema class.

It is part of the Teradata model, but it is conditionally populated.

Do not remove SandpitRecord.
Do not mark it as backlog.
Do not make it universal across Omnia.

Policy:
Database -> IS_SANDPIT -> SandpitRecord

Materialisation condition:
- source/platform is Teradata
- and at least one sandpit evidence field exists:
  sandpit_business_unit
  sandpit_owner
  sandpit_status

If sandpit fields are null, the Database still exists, but no IS_SANDPIT edge is materialised.

Update notes/descriptions only if needed to make this clear:
“Teradata-specific optional reference entity; conditionally populated from sandpit survey fields.”

Rerun:
python3 model_linkml/check_consistency.py
python3 model_linkml/scripts/convert_schema_to_visjs.py --validate-only
